            <ArticleTitle>[Electrode device for rheoperiodontography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>23-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The electrode device for rheoperiodontography is described. It enables a reliable fixing of a contact element on the mucosa and keeps dry mucosal surface under an elastic tip around the contact element, thereby providing more clear and consistent rheographic indices in any patient when using the technique. 28 patients suffering from dental plexalgia have been examined. The device is useful in neurology, neurostomatology, stomatology, and other similar fields for functional diagnosis of different diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
